-- the honesty condition on the medium's record: a constituent may be marked in excess over its mirror
-- image only if it has a mirror image to be in excess over, which is to say only if its own record carries
-- no improper symmetry. A record that marks water as being in excess is not wrong about water's
-- concentration; it is claiming a handedness that water does not have.
excess-honest : Dissolved → Material → Bool
excess-honest e k = case dis-excess e of
  false → true
  true → material-chiral k
